        </p>

        <div id="who-is-oma" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">1. Who Makes OMA Treadmills, and Does OMA Sell in the US?</h2>
<p>
            OMA treadmills are folding home machines sold under model numbers such as 1012EB, 1017EB, 5108EB,
            7200EB and 7200EA, along with incline models numbered 5925, 6134 and 6830. OMA’s own manuals, as
            copied by a manuals site, describe the company as having more than 20 years’ experience making
            fitness products. We could not find an OMA website for US buyers, a US address or a US support
            page.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>OMA does sell to US buyers.</strong> Four things show it. Third-party manual sites index
            OMA manuals against Amazon US product identifiers for the 1012EB/7200EB and the 7200EA. The
            OMA-7200EA has a US FCC equipment authorisation, the filing any electronic product sold in the US
            needs. A San Antonio, Texas, liquidation auction in August 2024 sold an OMA folding treadmill
            described as a customer return, with a stated retail price of $1,359.74. And marketplace resellers,
            including a fitness reseller whose listing has since been removed, have carried the 7200EB.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>OMA is also widely sold in Asia.</strong> OMA treadmills appear at Thai retailers such as
            HomePro and Supersports and on Bangladeshi classifieds, under model numbers such as 3201EB, 7418EA
            and 0061EB that we did not find offered in the US.
          </p>
          <p>
            In practice, then, buying an OMA treadmill in the US means buying through Amazon or a marketplace
            seller, with the seller’s returns terms and whatever warranty that listing states. That is the same
            position as most marketplace treadmill brands, and our guides to
            <a href="/zofdim-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Zofdim</a> and
            <a href="/ancheer-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">ANCHEER</a> describe brands in
            a similar position.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="oma-7200eb" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">2. The OMA 7200EB: What the Figures Say</h2>
<p>
            The 7200EB is the OMA treadmill searched for most by name. OMA’s manual covers it together with the
            1012EB, and its listings describe a folding treadmill with three manual incline settings, an LED
            console and a 300 lb capacity. Here is what the sources say.
          </p>
